    /**
     * Limit the amount of images per vehicle card by using the SRP max images option in AG Options
     *
     * Two fixes, 2026-08-21, hunting the DOM weight behind the keystroke-lag
     * reports:
     *
     * 1. This used to run only when a carousel first scrolled INTO VIEW, so
     *    every off-screen card kept its full slide stack in the DOM through
     *    every re-render - the trim only ever helped cards the shopper had
     *    already reached. It now also runs as part of the render rebuild
     *    (_buildSRPImageCarousel), so excess slides leave the DOM the moment
     *    the cards do exist, on every card, every render. Style recalculation
     *    and layout pay per node whether or not a card is on screen (unless
     *    content-visibility hides it, which older Safari lacks).
     *
     * 2. The gate was hard-coded "length > 5", which silently ignored a
     *    configured cap below five. It now gates on the cap itself.
     *
